ionality but other platforms (e.g., Access, SQL, presentation software) may be employed. A unique feature of this course will be applications drawn from the diverse program areas of the Dyson School: management; international development/trade; environment/resource economics; and food/agricultural economics. Case material will be contributed by the companies from the DUAC. Key topics will include: Optimization (Solver), Data graphing, Financial modeling, Ethical/social dimensions of IT, Forecasting, Pivot tables, Exponential smoothing, and Simulation.", "catalogBreadth": "", "catalogDistr": "", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "", "catalogWhenOffered": "Fall, spring, summer, winter.", "catalogComments": "", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "Enrollment required of and limited to Dyson/AEM majors in the Fall and Spring. Course is open to all non-Dyson majors during summer and winter session.", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": ["Provide students with the skills needed to employ spreadsheet modeling techniques for economic and management analysis."], "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "AG", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": null}, {"strm": 2650, "crseId": 350518, "crseOfferNbr": 1, "subject": "AEM", "catalogNbr": "2210", "titleShort": "Financial Accounting", "titleLong": "Financial Accounting", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "LEC", "ssrComponentLong": "Lecture", "section": "001", "classNbr": 1003, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "", "timeEnd": "", "startDt": "01/03/2017", "endDt": "01/21/2017", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 1, "netid": "eel33", "firstName": "Eric", "middleName": "E", "lastName": "Lewis"}], "pattern": "", "facilityDescr": null, "bldgDescr": null, "facilityDescrshort": nul